.TH FORGEKIT-CHECK 1 "2026-08-25" "ForgeKit 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forgekit-check \- Validate architectural conventions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forgekit check
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate architectural conventions of a ForgeKit project. Checks include
hexagonal architecture compliance, dependency direction, naming conventions,
and separation of concerns.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIformat\fR
Output format: human, json (default: human)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce output (except errors and JSON)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check current project:
.B forgekit check
.TP
Check with JSON output:
.B forgekit check --format json
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All checks passed
.TP
.B 1
Architectural violations found
.TP
.B 2
Execution error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./forge.yaml
Project configuration
.TP
.I ./.forge/features.yaml
Installed features
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forgekit (1),
.BR forgekit-analyze (1),
.BR forgekit-doctor (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ForgeKit Contributors <forgekit@demetrius-ch.github.io>